+Subject: hyper-transport and its driver answer from the address a datagram reached
+Why: A server bound to the unspecified address on a host with more than one address answered from its route's source, which a QUIC client does not accept from a server (RFC 9000 section 9): the driver hands hyper-transport each datagram's local address (kiln-rt's Arrival::to, from IP_PKTINFO), hyper-transport hands it to hyper-quic (Endpoint::handle_datagram_to, where handle_datagram passed None), and each transmit leaves from its src_ip (kiln-rt's Batched::send_segments_from). kiln goal 90 R2 (2026-11-21): adacachy held 192.168.1.77 beside its advertised 192.168.1.90, and every runner's direct link took no answer and fell to the HTTP tunnel, which dropped on each Wi-Fi blip.
